 * derivation must stay byte-identical or the two plugins stop sharing downloads.
 *
 * Divergence policy: cacheFile()/normalizeUrl()/sha256Hex() and everything that feeds the
 * FINAL <hash>.png target must stay byte-identical to TcgSharedNpcImageCache — that is what
 * makes the two plugins share one download. The writeDisk() temp-file suffix and the worker
 * thread name are deliberately NOT byte-identical: readDisk()/cacheFile() never reference a
 * .tmp path, so the temp suffix is not part of the cache key, and both plugins run in the
 * same JVM, so a shared suffix (or thread name) risks collisions/ambiguous thread dumps
 * without helping cache sharing. Do not "restore" these two for consistency with the
 * original — that would reintroduce the collision this divergence exists to avoid.
